    {
      "id": "KA-C71-another",
      "sequence": 2390,
      "title": "ಇನ್ನೊಂದು (innondu) — another one",
      "headword": "ಇನ್ನೊಂದು",
      "romanization": "innondu",
      "gloss": "another one",
      "script": "kannada",
      "modality": "voice",
      "derivedModality": "voice",
      "modalityReasons": [
        "no-visual-dependency"
      ],
      "sourceHash": "fnv1a64:cd136d070b4d7dd3",
      "notice": null,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "index": 0,
          "type": "warmup",
          "title": "Warm-up",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say what you think about something, out loud."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: ಇನ್ನೊಂದು",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಇನ್ನೊಂದು (innondu) — \"another one, one more\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Two pieces, both of them yours already: ಇನ್ನೂ (innū, \"still, yet\") and ಒಂದು (ondu, \"one\"). Push them together and the long vowel shortens: ಇನ್ನೊಂದು (innondu)."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಇನ್ನೊಂದು ಚಹಾ (innondu cahā) — \"another tea.\" That is what you say when the cup is empty and the answer is yes."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "grammar",
          "title": "Grammar Lens: one, and one more",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Pair it with plain ಒಂದು and you have the Kannada way of saying \"one … the other\":"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಒಂದು ಇಲ್ಲಿ, ಇನ್ನೊಂದು ಅಲ್ಲಿ (ondu illi, innondu alli) — \"one here, the other there.\""
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "There is no separate word for the other. Kannada counts: this one, and the one-more. It is the same trick the language uses everywhere — build the second thing out of the first rather than name it fresh."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "A second helping, and a way to talk about two things one at a time."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 4,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 1,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 1s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "ondu, then innondu",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: *ondu*, then *innondu*]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "innondu cahā",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: *innondu cahā*]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "ondu illi, innondu alli",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: *ondu illi, innondu alli*]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "RECALL",
              "instruction": "say innū, and say what it added to ondu",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU RECALL: say *innū*, and say what it added to *ondu*]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "RECALL",
              "instruction": "say mattu once more",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU RECALL: say *mattu* once more]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "RECALL",
              "instruction": "say hēḷu once more",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
