            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "RECALL",
              "instruction": "say ಮ once more",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU RECALL: say *ಮ* once more]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "RECALL",
              "instruction": "say anta once more",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU RECALL: say *anta* once more]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "RECALL",
              "instruction": "from much earlier — say kere, magu, snēhita, kuṭumba, and say what each one means",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU RECALL: from much earlier — say *kere*, *magu*, *snēhita*, *kuṭumba*, and say what each one means]"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 4,
          "type": "recall",
          "title": "Wrap-up Recall",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 3,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 3s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "How do you ask for that once more? (innondu sala hēḷi.) What does ಸಲ count? (Times.)"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "KA-C71-when",
      "sequence": 2410,
      "title": "ಯಾವಾಗ (yāvāga) — when?",
      "headword": "ಯಾವಾಗ",
      "romanization": "yāvāga",
      "gloss": "when?",
      "script": "kannada",
      "modality": "voice",
      "derivedModality": "voice",
      "modalityReasons": [
        "no-visual-dependency"
      ],
      "sourceHash": "fnv1a64:cd5c105086548692",
      "notice": null,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "index": 0,
          "type": "warmup",
          "title": "Warm-up",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: ask somebody to say it once more."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: ಯಾವಾಗ",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಯಾವಾಗ (yāvāga) — \"when?\""
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The question set is nearly complete: who, where, what, why, and now when. This is the last one an everyday exchange keeps reaching for."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಯಾವಾಗ ಬರುತ್ತೀರಾ? (yāvāga baruttīrā?) — \"when will you come?\" Notice the question ending on the end of it, doing the same job it did on ಗೊತ್ತಾ."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The answers are already yours: ಈಗ (īga, \"now\"), ನಾಳೆ, ನಾಡಿದ್ದು (nāḍiddu, \"the day after tomorrow\"). Ask ಯಾವಾಗ (yāvāga) and you can understand what comes back."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Five question words. Who, where, what, why, when — and a reason and an opinion to answer them with."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 1,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 1s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "yāvāga",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: *yāvāga*]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "yāvāga baruttīrā?",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: *yāvāga baruttīrā?*]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "answer it — īga, or nāḍiddu",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: answer it — *īga*, or *nāḍiddu*]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "RECALL",
              "instruction": "say yāke, then say yāvāga, and say which one asks for a reason",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU RECALL: say *yāke*, then say *yāvāga*, and say which one asks for a reason]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "RECALL",
              "instruction": "say athavā once more",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU RECALL: say *athavā* once more]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "RECALL",
              "instruction": "say ೇ once more",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU RECALL: say *ೇ* once more]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "RECALL",
              "instruction": "from much earlier — say beṭṭa, sahāya māḍu, kēḷu, tegeduko, and say what each one means",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU RECALL: from much earlier — say *beṭṭa*, *sahāya māḍu*, *kēḷu*, *tegeduko*, and say what each one means]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "RECALL",
              "instruction": "read ಅಲ್ವಾ, then say yāke",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU RECALL: read **ಅಲ್ವಾ**, then say *yāke*]"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 4,
