            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "What does ಯಾವಾಗ (yāvāga) ask? (\"When?\") Answer it with the word for \"now\". (īga.)"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "KA-S139-letter-va",
      "sequence": 2420,
      "title": "ವ (va) — one character, met inside words you already say",
      "headword": "ವ",
      "romanization": "va",
      "gloss": "the single character ವ — recognised inside words you already say",
      "script": "kannada",
      "modality": "pen",
      "derivedModality": "pen",
      "modalityReasons": [
        "writing-type",
        "writing-block",
        "script-block"
      ],
      "sourceHash": "fnv1a64:8f42545ff9a5470c",
      "notice": {
        "modality": "pen",
        "needs": [
          "a pen and something to write on",
          "your eyes, for letter shapes on the page"
        ],
        "waitUntilStopped": [
          "Script you'll notice: ವ",
          "Guided Practice"
        ],
        "text": "Before we start: this one needs your hands, so it is not a driving lesson. You will want a pen and something to write on and your eyes, for letter shapes on the page. You can listen to everything else now — leave the sections called Script you'll notice: ವ and Guided Practice until you have stopped, and I will say so again when we reach it."
      },
      "blocks": [
        {
          "index": 0,
          "type": "warmup",
          "title": "Warm-up",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 1,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 1s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: ◌ೇ — long or short?"
            },
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One character this time — and it is standing in the middle of the word for \"when\" and the word for \"or\" alike."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "script",
          "title": "Script you'll notice: ವ",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ವ — va."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "It is a consonant, and in this script a consonant is never bare: it comes with an a already in it. So it is not v, it is va. Kannada's v is the same sound that Tamil keeps at the front of many words where Kannada has turned it into b, which is why ಬಾ and ಬರೆ look nothing like their Tamil cousins."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "You already say these, and every one of them has ವ (va) somewhere inside it:"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಯಾವಾಗ yāvāga — when, from the lesson before this one."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಅಥವಾ athavā — or."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಹೂವು hūvu — a flower."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ದಯವಿಟ್ಟು dayaviṭṭu — please."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "writing",
          "title": "Writing: ವ",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Put your pen on ವ (va) and follow its line. Copy the shape you can see — slowly, and larger than it is printed."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "This book does not yet tell you where to start the character or which way to travel. That is a real thing, taught with real variation from school to school, and it is not written down here until it can be written down with a source. Copying what is in front of you needs no such source, and it is how the shape gets into your hand in the meantime."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 1,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 1s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "LOOK",
              "instruction": "at these words, and find ವ (va) in the ones that have it",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU LOOK: at these words, and find ವ in the ones that have it]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಯಾವಾಗ (yāvāga), ಅಥವಾ, ಹೂವು."
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "TRACE",
              "instruction": "ವ three times, saying va as you finish each one",
              "spoken": false,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU TRACE: ವ three times, saying *va* as you finish each one]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "LOOK",
              "instruction": "back at any page of this chapter and find ವ (va) once more",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU LOOK: back at any page of this chapter and find ವ once more]"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 4,
          "type": "recall",
          "title": "Wrap-up Recall",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 3,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 3s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Which character is this — ವ? What sound does it carry? (va.) Name one word you already say that contains it."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
